019a90f6-cb17-7083-abb2-09ab56cc366b,019a90f6-cb08-7211-9541-71d61e777b75,1,assistant,"To make panko crumbs, preheat your oven to 300 degrees F (150 degrees C). Then, tear pieces of white bread and push them through the shredding disk of a food processor to create coarse crumbs. Spread these crumbs on a baking sheet and bake in the preheated oven until they're dry but not toasted, which should take around 6 to 8 minutes. During baking, shake the sheet twice to help the crumbs dry evenly. Be careful not to let the crumbs brown. Once done, remove them from the oven and cool completely. You can then store the panko crumbs in an airtight container at room temperature.","{""type"": ""response"", ""model"": ""gpt-4-0613"", ""quality"": ""good"", ""original_id"": ""14844"", ""temperature"": 0.7}"
